    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** headlining the offensive unit. Boasting an elite 74.44 score, **Merrill** is the clear must-start, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Holmes (4.47 xERA) and a significant +13% boost from his favorable platoon split. Right behind him, **Cole Carrigg** (69.15) serves as our most intriguing play; he benefits from a massive +14% park factor, and his switch-hitting versatility against the lefty Bennett makes him an excellent volume producer for our categories. **Gunnar Henderson** (68.65) and **Coby Mayo** (66.72) also present strong value, as both look to feast on the generous 5.75 xERA of Aldegheri, effectively leveraging their platoon advantages to maintain high efficiency despite the inherent volatility of their aggressive approach.\n\nThe bench decision for this matchup was particularly nuanced, with **Nolan Schanuel** (51.38) narrowly missing the starting cut. While **Schanuel** carries a respectable projection, he ultimately fell short due to a suboptimal matchup against Bradish (3.60 xERA), which hampered his base score compared to the aggressive ceiling of our starting outfielders. We also considered **Nasim Nunez** (40.57), but his projection plummeted due to a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult face-off against the crafty Mayza, reinforcing our commitment to prioritizing higher-efficiency spots over raw speed potential in today's specific configuration. \n\nManaging risk remains paramount as we navigate this schedule. While the offensive outlook is bright, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.68) remains a marginal start today; his raw talent is tempered by an -17% penalty against Brown (3.31 xERA), creating a significant drag on his daily efficiency. We are monitoring the defensive alignment of **Drake Baldwin** (60.40) and **Josh Jung** (57.01) closely, as their scores are highly dependent on maintaining their middle-order placement. Barring any late-afternoon weather shifts, the Waves are positioned to capitalize on these specific pitching vulnerabilities while maintaining our rigid focus on efficient, high-OBP production across the 5x5 board.",
